# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository and on checkout.
#
# Without this rule the master index doubles in size every few commits. A Windows
# write turns llms.txt into CRLF (one CR per line); a later tool that treats a lone
# CR as a line terminator then rewrites it with LF only, and every CR becomes a real
# blank line. llms.txt went 257 -> 768 -> 1537 -> 3071 lines that way while its
# actual content stayed at ~173 lines, and "update one entry count" landed as a
# 768-insertion/257-deletion diff that made blame on the index useless.
#
# eol=lf (not just text=auto) is the half that matters: it pins the CHECKOUT, so a
# Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true cannot reintroduce the CRs.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must use LF line endings, or the shebang breaks on
# Git Bash/macOS/Linux with "bad interpreter: bash
".
*.sh text eol=lf
